            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Odoacer</strong><br>\nOdoacer was born around the year 433 A.D. into the Scirian tribe, which was part of the larger group of Germanic tribes. Little is known about his early years, but as a young man, he joined the Roman army. This was a common practice for Germanic warriors at the time as the Roman Empire recruited many soldiers from Germanic tribes.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Military Service</strong><br>\nDuring his military service, Odoacer demonstrated strong leadership skills and a capacity for strategy. He rose through the ranks to become a commanding officer. His service was during a time of great turmoil and decline for the Roman Empire, as it was losing territories and struggling to fend off invasions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Decline of Rome</strong><br>\nBy the mid-5th century, the Roman Empire was in a state of collapse. In 476 A.D., Odoacer led a revolt against the last Roman emperor of the west, Romulus Augustulus. After deposing the emperor, Odoacer decided not to take the title of emperor himself. Instead, he declared himself the King of Italy, effectively ending the Western Roman Empire.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
